  "warnings": [
    "locus 'ITS2' contains 5 distinct 5' and 2 distinct 3' termini, so one locus label is covering more than one primer pair. Not an error - but `locus` is what length filtering and reporting group by, and a quant carrying one primer pair only directly controls amplification for that pair. 5' groups: [ref_ancylostoma_ceylanicum, ref_ancylostoma_ceylanicum_pc, ref_ancylostoma_duodenale, ref_ancylostoma_duodenale_pc, ref_necator_americanus, ref_necator_americanus_pc]; [ref_ascaris_lumbricoides, ref_ascaris_lumbricoides_pc, ref_enterobius_vermicularis, ref_enterobius_vermicularis_pc, ref_toxocara_canis, ref_toxocara_canis_pc]; [ref_strongyloides_fuelleborni, ref_strongyloides_fuelleborni_pc, ref_strongyloides_stercoralis, ref_strongyloides_stercoralis_pc]; [ref_trichuris_incognita, ref_trichuris_incognita_pc, ref_trichuris_trichiura, ref_trichuris_trichiura_pc]; [ref_schistosoma_mansoni, ref_schistosoma_mansoni_pc]",
    "reference: no quant entries - copy-number estimation is unavailable and every negative will be an unverified negative",
    "the control tag has a 3-edit match inside 'pc_plasmid_backbone' (vector). Chance matches occur in a backbone of that length once indels are allowed. The risk is that a few non-specific backbone reads are misclassified, not that target reads are",
    "all 11 controls share one tag sequence - tag detection establishes that a read is control-derived, and the mapped locus establishes which control. This is expected, and noted so the two-step assignment is not mistaken for a bug",
    "index set i7: minimum edit distance is 2 but minimum Hamming distance is 4. The set tolerates 1 substitution(s) but only 0 indel(s) - so barcode matching must disable indels and rely on the tandem duplication for indel robustness",
    "index sets are only 1 substitution(s) apart at their closest (S502 CTCTCTAT vs N707 CTCTCTAC) - barcode search must be anchored on adapter context, never scanned across the read, or the two ends cannot be told apart",
    "run 'TITR01': no neg_extraction sample. No empirical detection threshold can be derived, so calls will fall back to the configured default and be flagged as such"
  ]
